-- An @export is given the ASSUMEs that its own body reads, and no others: a
-- request supplies them to the exported rule, and the rules it calls do not
-- see them.
-- So `via` is an error at its @export, because the ASSUME `rate` reaches it
-- only through `scaled`; `direct` reads `rate` itself and is published.
-- The error is reported by the export check, not the type check, so the file
-- still checks and the #EVAL at the end still runs.
ASSUME rate IS A NUMBER

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled` n MEANS n TIMES rate

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plain` n MEANS n PLUS 1

@export Read it directly
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`direct` n MEANS `plain` n PLUS rate

@export Reach it through a helper
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`via` n MEANS `scaled` n

#EVAL `plain` 3
